@startuml fig3_bridges
' Diagram 3 of the AIAS alignment: the bridges between the subdomains.
'
' Conventions: shared/FIGURES.md, with prefixes for the reason diagram 1 gives.
'
' What it shows: every relation and every equivalence this ontology adds, and
' nothing else. Read as a whole it is the answer to what the alignment
' actually states, as against what the four patterns state on their own.
'
' Four groups, one per question the alignment answers:
'
'   assignment   which resource performs which function
'   control      what a control acts on, and who performs it
'   data         which dataset a transmission carries
'   system       which resource takes part in a communication
'
' Left out on purpose: the class hierarchies of diagrams 1 and 2, and
' everything internal to the four patterns.

skinparam backgroundColor transparent
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 24
skinparam ranksep 48
skinparam padding 3
skinparam ArrowColor #1A2733
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowFontColor #1A2733
hide empty members
hide circle
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FCEFC7
  BorderColor #C9A227
  FontColor #1A2733
  FontSize 13
  BorderThickness 1
}

' ===================================================================
'  Which resource performs which function
'
'  VDI 3682 states the assignment from the process operator, which cannot
'  reach an AI function. aias:assignedFunction is what closes that gap.
' ===================================================================

class "vdi3682:Assignment" as Assignment
class "aias:Function"      as Function
class "aias:Resource"      as Resource

Assignment --> "*" Function : aias:assignedFunction
Assignment --> "*" Resource : vdi3682:assignedResource

' ===================================================================
'  What a control acts on
' ===================================================================

class "iso22989:Control"        as IsoControl
class "iec60050:Control"        as IecControl
class "vdi3682:ProcessOperator" as ProcessOperator

IsoControl -right- IecControl : owl:equivalentClass
IecControl --> "*" ProcessOperator : aias:actsOnProcessOperator

' ===================================================================
'  Which dataset a transmission carries
'
'  A relation rather than an equivalence. The payload of one transmission and
'  a collection of samples are not the same thing, and keeping them apart is
'  what lets a model ask which communications carry a given dataset.
' ===================================================================

class "iso7498:Association"      as Association
class "iso7498:ProtocolDataUnit" as Pdu
class "iso7498:UserData"         as UserData
class "iso22989:Data"            as Data

Association --> "*" Pdu      : iso7498:transmits
Pdu         --> "*" UserData : iso7498:hasUserData
UserData    --> "1" Data     : aias:carriesData

' ===================================================================
'  Which resource takes part in a communication
' ===================================================================

class "iso7498:OpenSystem" as OpenSystem
class "aias:Component"     as Component

Component   --> "*" OpenSystem : aias:appearsAsOpenSystem
Association --> "1" OpenSystem : iso7498:hasSourceSystem

' Layout only.
Assignment -[hidden]right- IsoControl
UserData   -[hidden]right- Data

@enduml
